{"question":"What did Pod Security Admission replace, and when was that removed?","answer_status":"answered","answer":"Pod Security Admission (the built-in PodSecurity admission controller) replaced PodSecurityPolicy (PSP). PSP was deprecated in Kubernetes v1.21 and removed in v1.25. The PodSecurity admission controller went alpha in v1.22, beta in v1.23, and stable in v1.25. Instead of PSP, you can use Pod Security Admission, a third-party admission plugin, or both.","evidence":[{"chunk_id":585,"document":"web:/docs/concepts/security/pod-security-policy/","title":"Pod Security Policies","section":null,"source_type":"docs_page","release_windows":[["1.25",null]],"claimed_status":null,"claimed_stage":null,"source_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/website/blob/8eb33afd12b1820c90a19c27d7a059006285c7e9/content/en/docs/concepts/security/pod-security-policy.md"},{"chunk_id":1242,"document":"web:/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/admission-controllers/","title":"Admission Controllers Reference","section":"What does each admission controller do? > PodSecurity {#podsecurity}","source_type":"docs_page","release_windows":[["1.25","1.25"]],"claimed_status":null,"claimed_stage":null,"source_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/website/blob/8eb33afd12b1820c90a19c27d7a059006285c7e9/content/en/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/admission-controllers.md"},{"chunk_id":511,"document":"web:/docs/concepts/security/pod-security-admission/","title":"Pod Security Admission","section":null,"source_type":"docs_page","release_windows":[["1.24","1.24"]],"claimed_status":null,"claimed_stage":null,"source_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/website/blob/98e2db7d9cc710554b486ad56274e362af03b438/content/en/docs/concepts/security/pod-security-admission.md"},{"chunk_id":4974,"document":"kep:2579","title":"KEP-2579: PSP Replacement Policy","section":"KEP-2579: Pod Security Admission Control > Implementation History","source_type":"kep","release_windows":[["1.22","1.24"],["1.24","1.25"],["1.25",null]],